    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0902" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.711/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-14T18:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>95. Your 171, March 12, 5 p.m. Department approves attitude outlined in paragraph
                    2 of your telegram. Please keep Department informed of further
                        developments.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d758-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d758-f1" n="57" xml:id="d758-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in China, in telegram No. 261, April 4, reported: “Following from
                    Tientsin, April 3, noon: Postal ban on the <hi rendition="#italic">North China
                        Star</hi> lifted today” (893.711/26).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
